# Phase 6: Public-Facing Community Site

## Goal
Build the public community site that replaces the TownPlanner-hosted site. Must be SEO-optimized, fast, and beautiful.

## Architecture
- Routes under `src/app/(public)/` using route group (no `/public` prefix in URL)
- ISR with 60-second revalidation on all public pages
- Lighter calendar component than FullCalendar (custom-built or minimal library)
- Tenant branding via CSS custom properties from `tenantBranding` table
- Community accounts via Clerk (separate from admin auth)

## Build Order

### 1. Public Layout & Branding
- `src/app/(public)/layout.tsx` — public layout with header nav, footer
- Header: logo, nav links (Events, Directory, Coupons, Blog, Videos), sign in/up
- Footer: operator info, social links, copyright
- Load tenant branding from Convex, apply as CSS variables:
  ```css
  :root {
    --brand-primary: var(--tenant-primary, #2563eb);
    --brand-logo: var(--tenant-logo);
  }
  ```

### 2. Homepage (`/`)
- Hero section with operator branding
- Featured events (next 3-5 upcoming)
- Featured businesses (top-tier advertisers)
- Latest coupons grid
- Recent blog posts
- All data fetched server-side with ISR

### 3. Event Calendar (`/events`)
- Interactive month/week/day calendar view
- Build with a lightweight approach (date-fns grid + custom components)
- Event cards on each day
- `/events/[id]` — event detail: name, description, times, location, associated business
- Category filter sidebar
- Search functionality
- `/events/submit` — event submission form (requires auth, submitted for admin approval)

### 4. Business Directory (`/directory`)
- Grid/list view of active advertisers
- Search by name, category
- Filter by category
- Sort by featured status (based on ad tier/purchases)
- `/directory/[slug]` — business detail: contact info, address, map, web link, coupons, events
- Map integration (Google Maps or Leaflet embed)

### 5. Coupons (`/coupons`)
- Grid of active coupons (endDate >= today)
- Each coupon card: image, title, business name, valid dates
- `/coupons/[id]` — coupon detail: full image, description, terms, download/print
- Claim button (requires account, tracks in `couponClaims`)
- Expired coupons auto-filtered out

### 6. Blog (`/blog`)
- Blog post list with featured image, title, excerpt, date, author
- Category filter
- `/blog/[slug]` — full post with SEO: meta title/description, OG image, JSON-LD structured data
- Blog editor at `/admin/blog/new` using Novel rich text editor
- Admin approval workflow for client-authored posts

### 7. Videos (`/videos`)
- Video gallery: grid of video cards
- YouTube/Vimeo embed support (parse URL, render embed)
- Category filter
- Associated business links

### 8. User Accounts
- `/auth/register` — community member registration
- `/profile` — user profile, event submissions, claimed coupons, favorites
- Clerk handles all auth UI components

### 9. SEO
- `generateMetadata()` on every page for dynamic meta tags
- OpenGraph images for blog posts and events
- JSON-LD structured data for events and businesses (LocalBusiness, Event schemas)
- `sitemap.xml` generation
- `robots.txt`

## Convex Tables for Phase 6
Add to schema: `coupons`, `couponClaims`, `blogPosts`, `videos`, `categories`, `tenantBranding`
Queries for public pages should NOT require auth — they read public data filtered by orgId.

## Performance
- Images: use `next/image` with proper sizing
- Bundle: avoid importing FullCalendar on public pages (use lightweight alternative)
- ISR: 60s revalidation keeps pages fresh without SSR cost
